ializes the full OpResult wrapper (`src/cli/render.ts:14-18`). A direct probe after build showed `node dist/cli.js view pull --file-path ... --json` printing `{ \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"value\\\": { \\\"messages\\\": [], \\\"meta\\\": ... } }`, not a top-level array. The process test reinforces the wrong contract by parsing OpResult via `parseResult`/`expectOk` and then unwrapping `.value` (`test/cli-process-view.test.ts:58-65`, `test/cli-process-view.test.ts:156-164`, `test/cli-process-view.test.ts:178-181`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/cli/view.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/cli/render.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-view.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.5\",\"TC-5.4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"S5-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"CLI pull/materialize stdout does not match the story contract\",\"evidence\":\"Story AC-5.5 and TC-5.4 require `view pull` to emit the JSON message array and `view materialize` to print the written path (`stories/05-render-targets.md:35-36`; `test-plan.md:47`). Production code instead routes both commands through `renderResult` (`src/cli/view.ts:140-141`, `src/cli/view.ts:172-186`), and `renderResult` serializes the full OpResult wrapper (`src/cli/render.ts:14-18`). A direct probe after build showed `node dist/cli.js view pull --file-path ... --json` printing `{ \\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"value\\\": { \\\"messages\\\": [], \\\"meta\\\": ... } }`, not a top-level array. The process test reinforces the wrong contract by parsing OpResult via `parseResult`/`expectOk` and then unwrapping `.value` (`test/cli-process-view.test.ts:58-65`, `test/cli-process-view.test.ts:156-164`, `test/cli-process-view.test.ts:178-181`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/cli/view.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/cli/render.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-view.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.5\",\"TC-5.4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocki